@startuml 11-seq-negotiation
!include _style.iuml
title xtxp.link content negotiation

participant "Client" as c
participant "xtxp.link\ngateway" as gw
participant "Directory" as dir
participant "Hosting node" as node

c -> gw : GET https://xtxp.link/{host}/{path}
gw -> dir : who hosts {host}/{path}?
dir --> gw : node + branch + latest vector

alt Accept: application/xtxp+xml
  gw -> node : open patch stream
  gw --> c : raw XTXP patch stream
else Accept: text/html
  gw --> c : rendered current state as HTML\n+ forms that POST edits\n+ link "open in native client" → xtxp://{host}/{path}
end

note over gw
  A server cannot tell whether an xtxp:// handler
  is installed, and a meta refresh to a missing
  handler fails silently, so the hand-off is a link.
end note

== deep link (syntax open) ==
c -> gw : GET /{host}/{path}?at={state vector}
gw --> c : the document exactly as it was at that vector

note over c, node
  /{host}/{path} is a native XTXP document hosted at {host}.
  /@/{domain}/{path} is a proxied overlay of an ordinary website.
end note
@enduml
